

1. Introductory Clause

RESPONSE:

This Loan Agreement (the "Agreement") is made on March 15, 2024, between Thinkplus Investments Limited, a company incorporated in England and Wales with company number 0123456789 and having its registered office at 123 Main Street, London, United Kingdom (the "Lender"), and Tech Innovations Limited, a company incorporated in England and Wales with company number 9876543210 and having its registered office at 456 Innovation Avenue, London, United Kingdom (the "Borrower").

The Lender has agreed to lend to the Borrower the sum of GBP 10,000,000 (the "Loan Amount") for the purpose of financing the Borrower's expansion into new markets (the "Purpose").

This Agreement is governed by the laws of England and Wales.

2. Representations and Warranties

2. Representations and Warranties

The Borrower hereby represents and warrants to the Lender as follows:

2.1 Authority

The Borrower has full power and authority to enter into and perform its obligations under this Agreement. The execution, delivery, and performance of this Agreement have been duly authorized by all necessary corporate action on the part of the Borrower.

2.2 Existence and Capacity

The Borrower is a duly incorporated limited company in good standing under the laws of England and Wales.

2.3 Authorized Borrower

The Borrower is the duly authorized borrower of the Loan Amount.

2.4 No Default

As of the date of this Agreement, the Borrower is not in default under any material agreement to which it is a party or by which it is bound.

2.5 Borrower's Assets

The Borrower owns or has the right to use and possess all assets necessary for the performance of its obligations under this Agreement.

2.6 No Liens

There are no liens, encumbrances, or other charges on the Borrower's assets that would affect the Borrower's ability to perform its obligations under this Agreement.

2.7 Financial Statements

The Borrower's financial statements presented to the Lender for the purpose of obtaining the Loan Amount are true and correct in all material respects.

2.8 No Conflicts

The execution, delivery, and performance of this Agreement do not violate any laws, regulations, or other legal restrictions applicable to the Borrower, or any material agreement to which the Borrower is a party or by which it is bound.

2.9 No Litigation

The Borrower is not a party to any litigation or governmental investigation that could reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on the Borrower's ability to perform its obligations under this Agreement.

2.10 Compliance with Laws

The Borrower has complied, and will continue to comply, with all applicable laws, regulations, and governmental requirements in connection with the Loan Amount and the performance of its obligations under this Agreement.

The Lender makes no representations or warranties, express or implied, other than as specifically set forth in this Agreement.

3. Covenants

3. Covenants

3.1 Borrower's Obligations

The Borrower covenants and agrees to the following:

3.1.1 Repayment of Loan

The Borrower shall repay the Loan Amount in accordance with the repayment schedule attached hereto as Schedule A.

3.1.2 Interest Payments

The Borrower shall pay the interest on the Loan Amount in accordance with the interest schedule attached hereto as Schedule B.

3.1.3 Financial Statements

The Borrower shall provide the Lender with accurate and complete financial statements, including balance sheets, income statements, cash flow statements, and statements of changes in equity, on a quarterly basis during the term of this Agreement.

3.1.4 Compliance with Laws

The Borrower shall comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and governmental requirements in connection with the Loan Amount and the performance of its obligations under this Agreement.

3.2 Lender's Obligations

The Lender covenants and agrees to the following:

3.2.1 Advance of Loan

The Lender shall advance the Loan Amount to the Borrower in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.

3.2.2 No Set-Off

The Lender shall not have the right to set off any amounts owed by the Borrower to the Lender against the Loan Amount or any interest or fees due under this Agreement.

3.3 Restrictive Covenants

3.3.1 Payment of Other Debts

The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, incur any indebtedness or obligation for borrowed money in excess of GBP 5,000,000.

3.3.2 Mergers and Acquisitions

The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, merge, consolidate, or sell a majority of its assets.

3.3.3 Restrictions on Dividends

The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, declare or pay any dividends or make any distributions of assets to its shareholders during the term of this Agreement, except for ordinary course of business dividends not exceeding GBP 500,000 per year.

3.4 Events of Default

The occurrence of any of the following events shall constitute an event of default under this Agreement:

3.4.1 Failure to Repay

The Borrower's failure to pay any amount when due under this Agreement.

3.4.2 Breach of Covenants

The Borrower's breach of any of its covenants, representations, or warranties under this Agreement.

3.4.3 Bankruptcy or Insolvency

The Borrower's filing for bankruptcy or insolvency, or the appointment of a receiver, trustee, or liquidator for the Borrower or any of its assets.

3.4.4 Litigation or Governmental Investigation

The Borrower's becoming a party to any litigation or governmental investigation that could reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on the Borrower's ability to perform its obligations under this Agreement.

3.4.5 Non-compliance with Laws

The Borrower's non-compliance with any applicable laws, regulations, or governmental requirements in connection with the Loan Amount or the performance of its obligations under this Agreement.

4. Loan Terms

4. Loan Terms

4.1 Amount

The Lender shall lend to the Borrower the sum of GBP 10,000,000 (Ten Million Pounds Sterling).

4.2 Currency

All amounts under this Agreement shall be payable in Pounds Sterling (GBP).

4.3 Maturity Date

The maturity date of the Loan Amount shall be March 15, 2027.

4.4 Repayment Schedule

The Borrower shall repay the Loan Amount, in equal installments of GBP 333,333.33 (Three Hundred Thirty-Three Thousand Three Hundred Thirty-Three Pounds Sterling and Three Pence), on the first day of each month, commencing on March 1, 2025, and ending on March 1, 2027.

4.5 Interest

The Borrower shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan Amount at a rate of 5% per annum (annual interest rate) calculated on a 360-day year, compounded semi-annually.

4.6 Fees

The Borrower shall pay a commitment fee of 1% per annum (annual commitment fee) on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan Amount, payable quarterly in arrears.

4.7 Security

The Borrower grants to the Lender a first priority security interest in all of the Borrower's assets, present and future, to secure the repayment of the Loan Amount, interest, and fees.

4.8 Borrower's Obligations

The Borrower shall maintain a current and valid insurance policy covering the Loan Amount and any collateral securing the Loan Amount, with a reputable insurance company approved by the Lender. The Borrower shall promptly notify the Lender of any changes to the insurance policy or collateral.

4.9 Lender's Right to Set Off

The Lender shall have the right to set off any amounts owed by the Borrower to the Lender against any amounts payable by the Lender to the Borrower under this Agreement.

4.10 Events of Default

The occurrence of any of the events of default set forth in Section 3.4 shall entitle the Lender to declare all amounts owing under this Agreement immediately due and payable.

4.11 Governing Law

This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales.

4.12 Jurisdiction

Any legal action or proceeding arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be brought exclusively in the courts of England and Wales.

4.13 Entire Agreement

This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes all prior negotiations, understandings, and agreements between the parties, whether written or oral, relating to the subject matter of this Agreement.

4.14 Amendments

This Agreement may not be amended or modified except by a written instrument executed by both parties.

4.15 Counterparts

This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument.

4.16 Binding Effect

This Agreement shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the parties and their respective successors and assigns.

