6. Default and Remedies

6. Default and Remedies

6.1 Default
A default under this Agreement shall occur if:

6.1.1 The Borrower fails to make any payment when due, including interest payments and fees.

6.1.2 The Borrower breaches any of its representations, warranties or covenants under this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within [INSERT CURE PERIOD] days after receiving notice from the Lender.

6.2 Remedies
Upon a default under this Agreement, the Lender shall have the following remedies:

6.2.1 Acceleration
The Lender may declare the entire outstanding principal amount of the Loan, together with all accrued and unpaid interest, fees, and other charges, immediately due and payable.

6.2.2 Security Interest
The Borrower hereby grants to the Lender a security interest in all of its present and future assets, and the Borrower shall execute such documents and do such acts as may be necessary or desirable to perfect and maintain the security interest.

6.2.3 Enforcement
The Lender may enforce its security interest in any manner permitted by law, including but not limited to the appointment of a receiver, the sale of the secured assets, or any other legal or equitable remedy.

6.2.4 Damages
The Borrower shall be liable to the Lender for any damages, costs, or expenses incurred by the Lender as a result of a default under this Agreement.

6.2.5 Legal Fees
In the event of a default, the Borrower shall be responsible for all reasonable legal fees and expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with enforcing its rights under this Agreement.

6.2.6 Waiver
No waiver by the Lender of any default or breach under this Agreement shall be effective unless in writing and signed by an authorized officer of the Lender. Any such waiver shall not operate as a waiver of any subsequent default or breach.

6.3 Cure
The Borrower may cure a default under this Agreement by paying all amounts due, including interest and fees, and complying with any other obligations required to cure the default. Upon cure, the Lender's rights to enforce its remedies shall be suspended, but not terminated, until there is a subsequent default.

